# Allowed extraction directives.  Built by check_extraction_directives.sh --list, then
# classified by hand; the gate beside it refuses anything else.  Six TAB-separated
# fields: FILE, KIND, LHS, RHS (the OCaml target, verbatim), CLASS, CONTRACT.
#
# Classes: repr, repr-proj, inherited, unreferenced, trusted.  See the header of
# check_extraction_directives.sh.  Only [trusted] replaces a computation, and only
# [trusted] carries -- and must carry -- a contract.
#
# The six trusted replacements in this tree, and where each one is:
#   safechecker-plugin/theories/Extraction.v  memo_trans, trans_memo_release
#     -- IN the shipped checker.  templateToPCUICShared.ml of the built 1a92b56c tree has
#        "let memo_trans = Trans_memo.memo" and "let trans_memo_release = Trans_memo.release".
#   utils/theories/canonicaltries/String2pos.v  ascii_cons_pos
#   common/theories/Transform.v                 time
#   utils/theories/MRUtils.v                    todo
#   template-rocq/theories/Extraction.v         Typing.guard_checking
#     -- NOT in the shipped checker: none of the 43 safechecker-plugin/src/*.ml of the
#        built 1a92b56c tree contains Char.code, Tm_util.time, failwith or fix_guard, and
#        string2pos.ml there holds only the [positive] datatype.  guard_checking IS in the
#        Template plugin (template-rocq/gen-src/typing0.ml:4147), which is loaded in the
#        same process but is not the safechecker.
#
common/theories/Transform.v	EXTRACT_CONSTANT	time	"(fun c f x -> let s = Caml_bytestring.caml_string_of_bytestring c in Tm_util.time (Pp.str s) f x)"	trusted	[time c f x] returns [f x]; its only other effect is to print a timing. NOT in the shipped safechecker: no safechecker-plugin/src/*.ml of the built 1a92b56c tree mentions Tm_util.time.
